//! @ai: generated
//! # volar-mxx-interop — the Volar-interop compiler for mxx
//!
//! Lowers a validated, frozen [mxx](https://github.com/MachinaIO/mxx) graph
//! (`mxx_ir_core::validate::ValidatedGraph`) into a `volar-compiler`
//! [`IrModule`], so `volar-spec` lattice elements can be *autogenerated*
//! from mxx DSL programs instead of hand-written. See
//! `docs/mxx-cutover-plan.md` (Phase 0).
//!
//! ## Shape contract
//!
//! - Typed IR only: the lowerer constructs `IrExpr`/`IrStmt` nodes; no
//!   pre-rendered Rust text (core design rule 1). The bundled runtime
//!   helpers (`rust_rt/mxx_rt.rs`) are plain spec-subset Rust parsed into IR
//!   through the same `parse_sources` pipeline as hand-written spec code.
//! - No `Vec` in emitted program structure (rule 11): an mxx frozen graph
//!   has all shapes concrete at validate time, so every emitted type is a
//!   fixed-size array. Runtime matrices are
//!   `[[[[u64; N]; D]; C]; R]` (row-major matrix of per-CRT-tower
//!   coefficient arrays).
//! - Deterministic (rule 5): sampler nodes are rejected as
//!   [`InteropError::Unsupported`] until they can be lowered onto explicit
//!   `SpecRng`-style tapes; only deterministic nodes lower.
//! - Loud coverage: every unsupported node kind fails with
//!   [`InteropError::Unsupported`] naming scope, node, and kind. Nothing is
//!   silently approximated.
//!
//! ## Phase-0 node coverage
//!
//! `Input` (non-artifact), `ConstantInt`, `ConstantBool`, `EvaluateInt`,
//! `IntBinary`, `IntCompare`, `BoolToInt`, `ConstantMatrix` (`Zero`,
//! `Identity`, `Polynomial` on scalar matrices), `MatrixBinary`
//! (add/subtract/multiply), `MatrixMulSmallRhs` (ordinary-multiply
//! semantics), `MatrixNegate`, `MatrixScale`, `Transpose`.

